    "collapsible_tabs_KLznyr": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_item_z4Djtt": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "High-Temperature Printing Methods and Materials",
            "content": "<p>Manufacturing high-temperature tapes and labels requires specific equipment, materials, and expertise.</p><p>The choice of printing technology significantly impacts the design and functionality of your labels, especially when dealing with high heat.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": true,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_33tqbd": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Printing Methods",
            "content": "<ul><li><strong>Thermal Transfer Printing:</strong> A common and versatile choice, it uses a special ribbon for high-heat resistance and adhesion</li><li><strong>Flexographic Printing:</strong> Offers good printability, but compatibility with label materials is crucial</li><li><strong>Digital Printing:</strong> A growing option, but ensure the printer and ink can handle high temperatures</li></ul><p><br/>The materials, including polyimide films, silicone adhesives, and other unique coatings, are chosen for their ability to endure extreme heat without degrading.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_KpRi8J": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Materials",
            "content": "<ul><li><strong>Polyimide (Kapton):</strong> Withstands high temperatures (up to 500°F) and harsh chemicals, making it a popular choice</li><li><strong>Polyester (PET):</strong> A more affordable option with good printability, ideal for temperatures up to 400°F</li><li><strong>Silicone:</strong> Highly heat resistant (up to 600°F) and flexible, but may not be suitable for high-resolution printing due to its softness</li></ul><p><br/>Doniger said that compatibility between the printing technology (inks, ribbons, plates) and the specific high-temperature tape or label material you’re using is crucial. This ensures your labels stay adhered to and function properly under extreme heat.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_3ja7Ly": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Choosing the Right High-Temperature Tape or Label",
            "content": "<p>Finding the ideal high-temperature tape or label requires considering several factors.</p><p>Doniger stresses the need to balance function and cost and recommends asking yourself the following questions:</p><ul><li><strong>What temperatures will the tape or label be exposed to?</strong> Short-term exposure to moderate temperatures (around 350°F) might allow for a more affordable option like high-temperature masking tape. For long-term high heat or harsh chemicals, Kapton polyimide film is a popular choice due to its superior durability and chemical resistance.</li><li><strong>What materials are you working with?</strong> Consider if the tape or label needs to conform around curves or odd shapes. Silicone adhesives offer high heat resistance and flexibility but may not be ideal for high-resolution printing.</li><li><strong>Do you need the tape or label to be printed on?</strong> Not all high-temperature materials can be printed on, but those that can allow for including logos, instructions, or even variable data like serial numbers or batch codes.</li></ul><p><br/>By considering these factors and consulting with specialists like the team at NADCO, you can ensure you select the most appropriate high-temperature tape or label solution for your application, optimizing performance and cost-effectiveness.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
